# Cell from playpick: mode=battleground map=flags spec=warlock:destruction
# style=mash view=1280x800 save=carried.
#
# Checked sessions.jsonl and direction.md's #7 first: `mash` has now run on
# exactly one battleground (2026-10-01-8, conquest, druid:feral, fresh) and
# read hits=0 the whole match because scripts/playbot.ts's want-computation
# has no steering branch for `mash` -- it releases the stick at the spawn
# point and round-robins ability slots 1-5 from wherever that is, forever.
# That reading was explicitly not treated as a game finding: a melee spec
# stranded at spawn has nothing in range to press into. This cell is the
# first chance to test the actual hypothesis under it -- is the zero-output
# shape about steering at all, or just about melee range? -- because
# warlock:destruction is ranged and Ebb and Flow's own spawn has shown
# bodies clustered close to the enemy team on this exact map before
# (2026-10-01-12's own druid:balance `good` pull died at fightTime=16 with
# the whole five-body party spawning right on top of Corvin). If a
# stationary ranged body can reach someone from its own spawn tile, `mash`
# should show nonzero hits despite never moving; if it still reads hits=0,
# that is a second, stronger data point that nothing spawns in spell range
# either, not just melee range.
open
shot front
targets

tap battleground
shot bg-menu
targets

